From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:43:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Drop decoded images no element shows beyond a budget

The document cached every image it ever decoded, by URL, for its lifetime:
scrolling a long list of images kept every one in memory, and the
renderers' own caches (which hold weak handles to free the images the
embedder drops) never saw them go. Images an element still shows stay;
of the rest, the most recently used are kept up to 16 MiB.
---
